    "fileId": 44763,
    "type": "Figure",
    "diagnosis": "Barrett dysplasia",
    "title": "",
    "legend": "Low-grade, intestinal type. Evenly spaced tubules are lined by enlarged, hyperchromatic, elongated, slightly stratified atypical cells with an increased number of mitoses and a lack of surface maturation.",
    "source": "",
    "copyright": "Odze RD",
    "tablehtml": "",
    "imageUrl": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/72/7/1314.jpg",
    "thumbnail": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/72/7/thumb_1314.jpg"
  },
  {
    "pkattachmentId": 75401,
    "bookid": 72,
    "chapterId": 7,
    "fileId": 44764,
    "type": "Figure",
    "diagnosis": "Barrett dysplasia",
    "title": "",
    "legend": "High-grade, intestinal type. Compact crypts with markedly enlarged, oval to elongated, hyperchromatic nuclei with multiple nucleoli, showing full-thickness stratification, an increased number of mitoses, loss of polarity, and pleomorphism.",
    "source": "",
    "copyright": "Odze Robert",
    "tablehtml": "",
    "imageUrl": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/72/7/1315.jpg",
    "thumbnail": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/72/7/thumb_1315.jpg"
  },
  {
